SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Page updated: Maine Judicial Branch Jury Stat
 us Notices
DESCRIPTION:This page's content changed since the last check. Visit the pa
 ge directly to review the update.\n\nWhat changed (text excerpt):\nAdded:\
 n  + All jurors selected for PANEL B\, State of Maine VS. Mark Azevedo\, A
 ND all regular GRAND JURORS\, please report to the Capital Judicial Center
  on Wednesday\, September 23\, 2026\, at 9:00 AM. No alternate Grand Juror
 s are needed for September. Thank you and have a pleasant evening.\n  + Se
 ptember 22\, 2026\n  + All Jurors who reported on 9/11/26\, except for the
  jurors on the State v Meierdirk panel\, should report to the second floor
  Jury Assembly Room at 10am on 9/23/26.\nRemoved:\n  - All jurors selected
  for Panel B\, State of Maine VS. Mark Azevedo\, please report to the Capi
 tal Judicial Center on Tuesday\, September 22\, 2026\, at 9:00 AM. Thank y
 ou and have a pleasant evening.\n  - September 21\, 2026\n  - All Jurors w
 ho were summonsed to appear on August 28th should appear on September 11th
  at 9:00am\, unless previously excused.\n  - Somerset County Superior Cour
 t - Skowhegan\n  - The following Jurors selected for Panel C in the matter
  of State vs Thompson\, need to appear on Monday\, September 21st\, 2026\,
  at 8:30am: #53\, #108\, #98\, #156\, #109\, #65\, #99\, #163\, #78\, #56\
 , #107\, #178\, #183\n  - You can park in the Skowhegan District Court\, S
 omerset Superior Court\, or the municipal parking lot. PLEASE DO NOT park 
 directly across from the Somerset Superior Court building. Thank you.\n  -
  PLEASE CHECK BACK HERE FOR ANY UPDATES TO THE ABOVE or CALL 1-800-872-553
 9 AFTER 6 PM THE NIGHT BEFORE YOU WERE TOLD TO REPORT.\n  - IF THE COURT N
 EEDS TO CLOSE DUE TO INCLEMENT WEATHER A MESSAGE WILL BE PL\n[diff truncat
 ed]\nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/juror/notice.shtml
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/juror/notice.shtml
